  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Oklahoma Has a Panhandle 🇺🇸🤔 No Man's Land",
    "description": "Why does Oklahoma 🇺🇸 have that long thin 'handle'? Blame the fight over slavery ⛓️ The Missouri Compromise banned slavery north of 36°30′. When Texas joined the US in 1845 as a slave state, it couldn't keep land north of that line, so in the Compromise of 1850 Texas gave it up 📜 The leftover strip, 166 miles long and 34 miles wide, belonged to no state or territory for 40 years: 'No Man's Land' 🤠 It finally joined Oklahoma Territory in 1890.",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "A strip of land that belonged to nobody for 40 years 🤯🤠",
      "Did you know this about Oklahoma? 👇",
      "Which weird state border next? 🗺️"
    ],
